{
  "name": "LAMELLA waveform wall panel",
  "scad": "src/waveform_wall.scad",
  "outdir": "exports",
  "previewdir": "previews",
  "_notes": [
    "max_bbox encodes the real manufacturing constraint: a tile must fit the",
    "bed. Printed back-down the tile's footprint is (width x height) and its",
    "printed height is (backing + relief), which is exactly the model bbox,",
    "so one box check covers all three axes.",
    "max_degenerate allows the collinear slivers CGAL emits where the",
    "backing's front plane meets a tile's top edge -- one inserted vertex per",
    "fin. They have zero area and leave the mesh watertight and genus-0.",
    "An assembled multi-tile artwork reports ONE connected body, not one per tile: adjacent tiles butt on exactly coincident planes, so loading the STL welds the shared vertices. That is confirmation the seams close with no gap and no overlap -- the tiles are still separate printed parts.",
    "Surprise mode rolls a new seed on every render, so its cases assert mesh validity only -- asserting a volume would be asserting on a coin toss. That it stays valid for ANY rolled seed is the point of the case."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "default_tile",
      "params": {
        "output": "Single tile"
      },
      "expect": {
        "watertight": true,
        "bodies": 1,
        "max_bbox": [
          180,
          180,
          180
        ],
        "max_degenerate": 80
      }
    },
